content:
Maya: ClearLens onboarding alert. We're seeing a sudden preflight surge when they run CI + deploy their SPA. 429s spike right after deploys and during feature-flag rollouts. Any ideas?
Jon: likely a stampede: CI jobs + multiple browser tabs + service-worker background sync all triggering preflight/ephemeral refresh simultaneously. Can you share their init pattern?
ClearLens-Dev: simplified flow:
```js
// app init
await Promise.all([preflight(), warmCache(), preloadAssets()]);
// service worker
self.addEventListener('fetch', e => { if (shouldWarm(e)) fetch('/api/preflight', { headers: { 'x-client-id': 'clearlens-web-2' } }); });
// CI runner
curl -H "x-client-id: clearlens-ci-1" /api/preflight || true
```
Alec: three quick problems: 1) parallel preflight calls during page cold-start, 2) SW duplicates when tabs open, 3) CI runners doing many short-lived calls from many IPs.
Maya: they also rotate ephemeral tokens aggressively in CI which multiplies the effect.
Jon: client fixes we recommend: 1) coalesce token fetches so only one inflight per app process/tab, 2) debounce SW preflight using clients.matchAll(), 3) avoid preflight in CI - reuse token per job. Example coalesce snippet:
```js
let inflight = null;
function getEphemeral(){
  if (inflight) return inflight;
  inflight = fetch('/auth/ephemeral').finally(()=> setTimeout(()=> inflight = null, 30_000));
  return inflight;
}
```
Maya: infra/ops options: short warmup capacity bump for 24h and mark CI client IDs so we can treat them with a special shaping policy. OnboardBot can you open a temporary warmup ticket?
OnboardBot: Created ticket #CLEAR-ONB-77 for temporary warmup capacity (24h), owner: Alec, ETA: 60m.
Alec: also suggest they add x-client-id on all preflight requests (they already do) and include x-app-version. More important: have CI set x-client-type: ci-job so we can apply per-client rules instead of per-IP.
ClearLens-Dev: done. We patched CI to reuse a job-scoped token and set x-client-type: ci-job.
Jon: extra tip: set Access-Control-Max-Age >= 600 on the preflight endpoint to reduce browser OPTIONS frequency — especially useful since they send custom headers.
Maya: they can also move client-id into the ephemeral token payload to avoid custom headers on hot path.
ClearLens-Dev: after changes we measured: preflight attempts dropped from ~300/min to ~22/min in the first 10 minutes. Sample logs: 
[2026-11-09T02:05:01Z] preflight clearlens-web-2 200
[2026-11-09T02:05:12Z] preflight clearlens-web-2 429
[2026-11-09T02:05:40Z] preflight clearlens-web-2 200 retry
Alec: great. CS handoff checklist to send to customer: ["coalesce ephemeral token fetch per tab","debounce service-worker preflight using clients.matchAll()","reuse token in CI jobs","set headers: x-client-id, x-client-type, x-app-version","set Access-Control-Max-Age >= 600","ops ticket CLEAR-ONB-77 active for 24h","monitor warmup dashboard 2h and rollback plan"].
Maya: I'll message ClearLens with the checklist and offer a small SDK helper to opt-in token coalescing + SW guard.
ClearLens-Dev: please also note CI runners were behind a NAT pool, we flagged that with infra to avoid per-IP shaping. Thanks all, will confirm once stable for 2h. :white_check_mark:
